<article class="env-definition" id="0G0I">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G0I">Definition <span data-tag="0G0I">57.15.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X \to S$ and $Y \to S$ be smooth proper morphisms. An object $K \in D_{perf}(\mathcal{O}_{X \times _ S Y})$ is said to be <em>the Fourier-Mukai kernel of a relative equivalence from $X$ to $Y$ over $S$</em> if there exist an object $K' \in D_{perf}(\mathcal{O}_{X \times _ S Y})$ such that </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Delta _{X/S, *}\mathcal{O}_ X \cong R\text{pr}_{13, *}(L\text{pr}_{12}^*K \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_{X \times _ S Y \times _ S X}}^\mathbf {L} L\text{pr}_{23}^*K')  \]
</div>
  <p> in $D(\mathcal{O}_{X \times _ S X})$ and </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \Delta _{Y/S, *}\mathcal{O}_ Y \cong R\text{pr}_{13, *}(L\text{pr}_{12}^*K' \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_{Y \times _ S X \times _ S Y}}^\mathbf {L} L\text{pr}_{23}^*K)  \]
</div>
  <p> in $D(\mathcal{O}_{Y \times _ S Y})$. In other words, the isomorphism class of $K$ defines an invertible arrow in the category defined in Section <a href="/tag/0G0F" data-tag="0G0F">57.14</a>. </p>
</article>